Write a Python program to calculate the square root of a number (the example uses num = 8).
import math
num = 8
square_root = math.sqrt(num)
print(f"The square root of {num} is {square_root}")

Find the square root of a real or complex number using Python's cmath module (the example uses 1+2j).
import cmath
complex_num = 1 + 2j
sqrt_complex = cmath.sqrt(complex_num)
print(f"The square root of {complex_num} is {sqrt_complex}")
